   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **the man in me** (1 review): The opening number was a cover of Bob Dylan's song from the movie [4]\n- **lowdown** (1 review): Reviewers highlight the performance of this track as particularly strong [2]\n- **the way that he sings** (1 review): The rendition of this specific song is singled out as excellent [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **the man in me**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **how do you know**: rare: 10 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2004-06-18.shnf** (recommended): source not stated; 17 songs; 115 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: The audio quality is described as superior to other popular recordings of the band; Minor league baseball fireworks create small popping noises audible in the background; Occasional public address system issues are noted within the recording [1][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: lebowski [1]\n- Band members performed in costumes representing characters from the film The Big Lebowski [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2004-06-18.shnf**: taped by Jon Ice; transferred by Jon Ice; source: ck61 > Active Cables > JK Labs DVC > Apogee Mini-Me > Powerbook G4 @ 24/48 with Spark XL v2.8 [1]",
